  "track.arch.m.god.title": "An Activity that does everything, put through four tests",
  "track.arch.m.god.overview": "The ClinicBook app's Choose a time screen is written two ways: (1) the Activity calls the network, parses JSON, caches and draws the UI itself; (2) it is split into UI, ViewModel, repository and data source. Both work the first time. We put them through four tests: a tap, a rotation, a server API change, and writing a test.",
  "track.arch.m.god.wrapup": "Architecture does not make the app work better on the first tap. It decides what happens next: whether data survives a rotation, how many files one change spreads to, and whether you can test on your machine or need a device. The root principles are separation of concerns and not keeping data in components the system can destroy at any time.",
  "track.arch.m.god.simp.1": "The diagram shows four layers for clarity; the official guide requires only UI and data at minimum (chapter G2). The number of files to change is counted in the sample app (three screens calling the free-slot API).",
  "track.arch.m.god.simp.2": "Rotation and ViewModel behaviour follow the official docs; the site does not run a real app.",
  "track.arch.m.god.ctl.hint": "Switch the approach and walk again; compare the three metrics at the last step.",
  "track.arch.m.god.ctl.case": "Approach",
