  "track.arch.m.events.lost.na": "not yet",
  "track.arch.m.events.lost.no": "no",
  "track.arch.m.events.lost.yes": "yes",
  "track.arch.m.events.truth.flag": "a state flag nobody clears",
  "track.arch.m.events.truth.stream": "an event stream without replay",
  "track.arch.m.events.truth.state": "UI state, with a clear function",
  "track.arch.cap.events": "A loop: the Activity sends the tap up to the ViewModel, the ViewModel puts state or an event into the channel, the channel brings it back to the Activity, the Activity shows the message. A red-outlined box is where the message repeats or gets lost. The \"Timeline lanes\" tab shows the old and new Activity step by step.",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s1.title": "Tap Book: the ViewModel sets showSuccess",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s1.explain": "repo.book() finishes and the ViewModel sets showSuccess = true in its StateFlow. The collecting Activity receives the new state and shows the Toast \"Booked for 9:00\". Nobody sets the flag back to false.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.sticky.s1": "Tap Book: the ViewModel sets showSuccess",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s2.title": "Rotate: a new Activity, the same ViewModel",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s2.explain": "The system destroys and recreates the Activity. The ViewModel survives the recreation, so its state is intact, showSuccess = true included.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.sticky.s2": "Rotate: a new Activity, the same ViewModel",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s3.title": "The new Activity collects: the Toast shows again",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s3.explain": "StateFlow replays its latest value to a new subscriber. The new Activity receives the state with showSuccess = true and shows the Toast a second time, although the user booked nothing new.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.sticky.s3": "The new Activity collects: the Toast shows again",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s4.title": "It repeats on every configuration change",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.sticky.s4.explain": "Rotate again, change the font size, switch light/dark: every time the Activity is recreated, \"Booked\" shows again. The bug is that the message is kept as a state that lasts forever.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.sticky.s4": "It repeats on every configuration change",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s1.title": "Tap Book: the request is running",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s1.explain": "The ViewModel calls repo.book() in viewModelScope. When done it will emit \"booked\" into a MutableSharedFlow() with no replay and no buffer.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.shared.s1": "Tap Book: the request is running",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s2.title": "Rotate midway: nobody is collecting",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s2.explain": "The old Activity is destroyed and stops collecting; the new one has not started collecting yet. For a short window the event stream has no subscriber.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.shared.s2": "Rotate midway: nobody is collecting",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s3.title": "The request finishes right then: the emit is dropped",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s3.explain": "With a MutableSharedFlow() without replay, emitting with no subscribers returns at once and the value is not stored anywhere. The \"booked\" event is gone.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.shared.s3": "The request finishes right then: the emit is dropped",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s4.title": "The new Activity receives nothing: the user books again",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.shared.s4.explain": "The new Activity starts collecting but the event is already gone. The user sees no confirmation, thinks the booking failed, taps again and ends up with two appointments.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.shared.s4": "The new Activity receives nothing: the user books again",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s1.title": "Tap Book: the message goes into UI state",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s1.explain": "repo.book() finishes and the ViewModel sets userMessage = \"Booked for 9:00\" in UI state. The screen sees a non-null userMessage and shows a Snackbar.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.state.s1": "Tap Book: the message goes into UI state",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s2.title": "Shown: the UI reports back, the ViewModel clears it",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s2.explain": "When the Snackbar closes, the UI calls vm.messageShown(). This is a user event like any other: the ViewModel updates state, userMessage = null.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.state.s2": "Shown: the UI reports back, the ViewModel clears it",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s3.title": "Rotate: nothing repeats",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s3.explain": "The new Activity receives the current state from the StateFlow, but that state has no userMessage. The screen matches what is true: no message is pending.",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.state.s3": "Rotate: nothing repeats",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s4.title": "Variant: rotate before it could show",
  "track.arch.m.events.s.state.s4.explain": "If the rotation happens right after userMessage is set, the old Activity is destroyed before showing it. The message is still in state, so the new Activity receives it, shows it exactly once, then reports messageShown().",
  "track.arch.m.events.ev.state.s4": "Variant: rotate before it could show",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.try": "Walk the four steps of each approach; count how often the message showed at the last step.",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.sticky.s2": "State holders: a ViewModel keeps its state and operations across Activity recreation. [[src:ax-stateholders]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.sticky.s3": "kotlinx.coroutines 1.11.0: a StateFlow always has a value and replays the most recent one to new subscribers. [[src:kx-stateflow-api]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.sticky.s4": "A \"succeeded\" flag is an event held as a lasting state. The fix is not to drop state, but to let the UI report back and clear it (the third approach).",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.shared.s2": "UI events: when the ViewModel outlives the UI (as during rotation), Channels and other streams do not guarantee the event is delivered and processed. [[src:ax-ui-events]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.shared.s3": "kotlinx.coroutines 1.11.0: MutableSharedFlow() has no replay or buffer; emit returns immediately when there are no subscribers. In the absence of subscribers only replay values are kept. [[src:kx-sharedflow]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.shared.s4": "This is why the docs call losing events an unacceptable experience: the user may miss critical information or leave the app in an inconsistent state. [[src:ax-ui-events]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.state.s2": "UI events: the user having consumed the message (dismissing it or after a timeout) is treated as user input, and the ViewModel needs to know so it can update state. [[src:ax-ui-events]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.state.s3": "Even though the message is transient, the UI state faithfully describes the screen at every point: the message is shown, or it is not. [[src:ax-ui-events]]",
  "track.arch.m.events.co.state.s4": "Docs: turning ViewModel events into UI state makes them reproducible after configuration changes and guarantees UI actions are not lost; to survive process death as well, use SavedStateHandle. [[src:ax-ui-events]]",
